  "question": {
    "text": "An expression for a dimensionless quantity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>; where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are constants, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is distance; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is Boltzmann constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is the temperature. Then the dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be&nbsp;"
  },
